  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">V&#xe4;rldsbanken-GPOBA m&#xf6;drav&#xe5;rdskuponger 2012-18</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WB-GPOBA maternal health voucher proj. 2012-18 - WB-GPOBA maternal health voucher proj. 2012-15</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Output Based Aid &quot;kuponger&quot; f&#xf6;r m&#xf6;drav&#xe5;rd som subventionerar          kostnaden f&#xf6;r gravida kvinnor och nyblivna m&#xf6;drar till kvalitativ     h&#xe4;lsov&#xe5;rd. Programmet genonf&#xf6;rs i samarbete med V&#xe4;rldsbanken</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Based Aid voucher programme for maternal care to subsidy the   cost of access to quality ante-natal, maternal and post-natal care    for pregnant and newly delivered mothers and their babies. The        project is implemented in cooperation with the World Bank GPOBA.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Uganda Reproductive Health Voucher Project (URHVP) was a four-year program (2015-2019) implemented by Marie Stopes Uganda (MSU) on behalf of the ministry of Health,&#xa0;in 25 districts of South-western and Eastern Uganda.

The main development objective of the project was to increase access to safe delivery services for marginalized women living in rural and disadvantaged areas during pregnancy and delivery.</narrative>
  </description>
